Hmm, what do you want the ODSM for? Sleep resistance can be had in so 
many other ways... Or is orange just your favourite colour?

Me, without any style-issuews, would go for the Snickersnee / Silver 
Saber combo. Or Snickersnee and the starting Katana. That should cut up 
stuff pretty good.

IMHO there's really no need to get Grayswandir.

I recently ascended a Tsurugi wielding Samurai (on the tournament 
server, yay! :), who had his starting Katana and Wakizashi until 
Ashikaga-baka was killed by those. Snickersnee I had also, but just 
carried it around, since it is a nice sword.

The thing about the Tsurugi is twofold:
a) It's your Quest Item, so Rodney will steal it from you (or at least 
try to). So, you'd best keep some backup swords with you, or some 
death-rays...
b) It's a twohanded weapon, so if it ever does get cursed, your a in a 
bit of a bind, since you can't easily uncurse it (well not as easy as 
other stuff). It does have a rather high chance to resist curses though 
and the occasional double damage, resp. insta-kill is nice too.

Damagewise, nothing beats #twoweaponing Grayswandir and something else, 
but my first ascension (Valkyrie), had Excalibur and a found Katana, my 
first Samurai ascension, IIRC, had Snickersnee and the starting Katana 
and that was pretty powerful.

Armorwise, I'd go for GDSM and the AoReflection. Maybe switch to AoLS 
when going against Ashikaga-baka, to guard against bisecting... Or just 
death ray him or something.

The shield is not something I'd use, esp. when able to #twoweapon. When 
not, the shield and a Yellow DSM plus a CoMR would be a nice Idea, but 
then I don't know what weapon I'd use, probably Snickersnee...
